  "strategy": "The first several turns are mana: a Signet, Rampant Growth, Kodama's Reach, an Explore for the extra land drop. Aesi arrives on turn six and converts the whole plan into cards - every land after that draws one, and Aesi lets you play two. The top end is Leviathans that the deck's own Islands make unblockable: Stormtide Leviathan turns off the ground entirely, and Slinn Voda kicked clears the board of everything that is not one of yours.",
  "signature": [
    {
      "card_id": "avenger_of_zendikar",
      "why": "Turns a board full of lands into a board full of creatures in one cast."
    },
    {
      "card_id": "stormtide_leviathan",
      "why": "Makes every land an Island, so it is unblockable and nothing on the ground may attack."
    },
    {
      "card_id": "rampaging_baloths",
      "why": "Every land after this one is a 4/4."
    },
    {
      "card_id": "seer_s_sundial",
      "why": "Two mana a land, over and over, for as long as the game runs."
    }
  ]
